                                        Recursion
->Recursion has no such benefit in performance, infact loops are sometime better for performance
Every recursive function has 2 parts: Base case and recursive case
    Base case is when function doesn't call itself
    Recursive case is when function calls itself

Call Stack:It is a region of memory that manages function execution
WHenever a function is called, it creates a stack frame(activation record) for that function
the stack frame generally contains: parameters,local variables,return addresses
upon completion of funciton, the stack frame is popped from the call stack

Stack overflow:
    Every stack frame consumes some stack space, sometime the stack space will exhaust

When you called a function from another function,the calling function is paused in a partially completed state.


